+**Where the trap lives, measured.** The adjective *extra-skeletal* is in that trial's posted
+eligibility criterion, not in its title or its listed conditions, so the two screens separate by
+reading depth. Over the four adjudicated records, a histology-name screen restricted to titles and
+listed conditions never fires at all; extended across the posted criterion it fires exactly once,
+on the refusal, for a precision of 0.00. A combined histology-and-molecular lexicon loses precision
+the same way, 0.67 to 0.50, when the criterion text is added. Reading eligibility criteria protects
+a reader, not a string matcher: for the one term a patient is most likely to type -- the name of
+their own histology -- deeper string reading creates the false hit rather than preventing it.
+Denominator four records; not a sample of the registry.
 
